age models of protein sequences are scaled up to 15 billion parameters, an atomic-resolution picture of protein structure emerges in the learned representations. This results in an order-of-magnitude acceleration of high-resolution structure prediction, which enables large-scale structural characterization of metagenomic proteins. We apply this capability to construct the ESM Metagenomic Atlas by predicting structures for &gt;617 million metagenomic protein sequences, including &gt;225 million that are predicted with high confidence, which gives a view into the vast breadth and diversity of natural proteins.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1126/science.ade2574", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2023, 3, 16]], "date-time": "2023-03-16T13:58:26Z", "timestamp": 1678975106000}, "is-referenced-by-count": 6201, "title": ["Evolutionary-scale prediction of atomic-level protein structure with a language model"], "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0883-1373", "authenticated-orcid": true, "given": "Zeming", "family": "Lin", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "FAIR, Meta AI, New York, NY, USA."}, {"name": "New York University, New York, NY, USA."}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1666-3223", "authenticated-orcid": true, "given": "Halil", "family": "Akin", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "FAIR, Meta AI, New York, NY, USA."}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4412-3742", "authenticated-orcid": true, "given": "Roshan", "family": "Rao", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "FAIR, Meta AI, New York, NY, USA."}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3224-8142", "authenticated-orcid": true, "given": "Brian", "family": "Hie", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "FAIR, Meta AI, New York, NY, USA."}, {"name": "Stanford 